# dnf — real-world examples

## Install the latest version of a package

```sh
dnf install <package_name>
```

## Search package details for a string

```sh
dnf search <string>
```

## Find which package provides a binary

```sh
dnf provides <path_to_binary>
# e.g.
dnf provides /usr/bin/htop
```

## With dnf-plugins-core installed

```sh
# Download an RPM without installing it
dnf download <package_name>

# Install build dependencies from an SRPM or .spec file
dnf builddep <srpm_or_spec_file>
```

## Everyday maintenance

```sh
dnf check-update      # what has updates
dnf upgrade           # apply them
dnf remove <package>  # uninstall
dnf history           # transaction log
```

## Rosetta: dnf → zypper (OpenSUSE Tumbleweed at home)

| dnf                    | zypper                  |
| ---------------------- | ----------------------- |
| dnf install pkg        | zypper install pkg      |
| dnf search str         | zypper search str       |
| dnf upgrade            | zypper dup  (Tumbleweed)|
| dnf remove pkg         | zypper remove pkg       |
| dnf repolist           | zypper repos            |
